<title>HUNGARY: Konzum sells unprofitable operations.</title>
<headline>Konzum sells unprofitable operations.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian retailer Konzum Rt has sold its stakes in three subsidiaries to get rid off unprofitable operations, a company official told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The stakes are worth a total nominal 50.8 million forints and we sold them for 42.6 million forints,&quot; Konzum's deputy finance director Maria Ozsvath said. &quot;These were unprofitable investments.&quot;</p>
<p>Konzum sold its 100 percent stake in  Szoloskert Vendeglatoipari Kft, and its 50 percent stake in each of Helkon Ruhaipari Kft and  Jakon-Auto Kft.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
